From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Seabraid <seabraid@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 1 Jan 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 06/16] SEABRAID_STRATA_HOT_SHARE: opt-in f-paced interleave
 gives the helper GPU a share of the HOT experts

Today the primary cache takes the top of the expert ranking and seabraid_open gives the helper "ranked
order, nothing the primary holds" - the colder tail. Routing is skewed: in the IQ3_S all-VRAM run the
3090 held 45% of the experts (11,110 of 24,576) but did 13.6% of the expert work.

SEABRAID_STRATA_HOT_SHARE=<f in [0,1]>|auto (unset = today's fill, bit for bit) walks the ranking hottest-first
and deals pair n to the helper when floor((n+1)f) > helper picks so far, until one side's budget is
full; then the other side takes the following ranks until it is full. "auto" is the helper's share of
both byte capacities. The primary sizes and fills from its picks only (hot_order); `profile` keeps the
true ranking, which the helper walks (skipping what the primary holds, so it lands on its picks first)
and which the RAM copy, K/V refills and heat ranks keep reading.

The helper's capacity is known before the primary decides: its preflight free figure (the same header
field seabraid_open sizes from) less 512 MiB, its own 256-byte blob rounding, and its slot count - the
arithmetic seabraid_open uses. The primary's cost/budget are the sized-slot loop's own.

Disjointness: at load it stays seabraid_open's own primary.slot_of check, and a startup line counts the
pairs both caches hold and refuses to start if any. STRATA_DISJOINT_ADAPT is forced on with hot share
(the adaptive tier would otherwise promote the helper's hot experts into the primary). Refused, not
ignored, with a layer split, more than one helper tier, --peer-device, --expert-cache-per-layer,
--remote-expert-opt, STRATA_EXPERT_NIBBLE or --retier.

Host test: tests/program/seabraid_hot_share_test.cpp re-enacts the primary's sized-slot loop and
seabraid_open's walk: disjoint, helper lands on its planned picks, f=0 equals today's prefix, top-2000
ranks split f within one pair. Not run on a GPU.
